WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
The authors ablate two design choices: the balance
factor alpha that weights answer loss against explanation loss,

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:09.260
and the choice of explanation generator.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.930
On GQA-REX,

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:18.600
the LSTM variant ranges from about seventy-five to
seventy-seven and a half percent across different alpha values,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.270
and the Transformer decoder at alpha equal to one
half reaches seventy-seven point zero six percent.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:27.940
On VQA-E,

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.610
every configuration lands within a fraction of a
percent of the seventy-one and a half percent baseline.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:37.280
The takeaway from these sweeps is that answer
accuracy is remarkably stable no matter

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.950
how the explanation loss is weighted or which
decoder architecture generates the explanation,

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.620
so the explanation module can be added essentially
for free.
